OL,3,GNEWSAMeet the super-sniffer whose nose
OL,4,Acan save lives
OL,5,
OL,6,FMany people with a finely attuned sense
OL,7,Fof smell choose to become experts in
OL,8,Fthe delicate bouquets of fine wines,
OL,9,Fperfumes or coffee.
OL,11,FNot James Dyson.
OL,13,FInstead, he makes a living as a
OL,14,Fprofessional "gas sniffer", detecting
OL,15,Fthe nasty niff of rotten eggs that can
OL,16,Falert us to potentially deadly leaks.
OL,18,FDyson is one of four rhinologists - to
OL,19,Fgive them their official title -
OL,20,Fworking for Cadent, which supplies
OL,21,Fnatural gas to 2.7 million homes and
OL,22,Fbusinesses in north-western England.
